00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:26.500
Because there were even points where I was trying to find a skate shop and there was never those doors never led anywhere like that.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:34.280
And then I only until I stopped avoiding the people skating around that I realized, like, oh, I could just talk to these people.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.800
Like, that's one of those guys is Rodney.

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:45.940
Right. I mean, you guys are talking about whether or not, like, it explains what's happening or whatever.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:49.700
But you have to remember, too, it's just like this is the second game in this franchise.

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:53.560
And they've done the classic NES thing of just like, nope, totally different game.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.480
Like, whatever you thought Skate or Die was, it's different now.

00:15:56.780 --> 00:16:07.580
This is not like Skate or Die 1, which was just like, I don't know, you know, it had like a little bit of a hub thing that you, like, skated around to go to different mini games, essentially, and do skateboard things there.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:13.140
You could do the high jump or skateboarding race or joust or the half pipe.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:19.260
This is like an adventure game, like with with levels and like open world.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:21.460
You know what I mean, though?

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.480
It's like it just drops you in there.

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.520
And I don't think if, you know, like, who knows?

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:32.920
Maybe back then people would just buy Skate or Die 2 and not have to, you know, like not care whether or not.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:34.880
Right. So maybe this was their entry into it.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.100
And then they go back to Skate or Die 1 and like, oh, this is weird.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:42.620
But you have to imagine there's some section of the of the audience that was like, oh, I really enjoyed Skate or Die 1.

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:44.500
I want to see how they improved on it.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.100
And now it's like a totally different game.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:54.400
Yeah. Now that one is equivalent to it would be equivalent to like us in the in the late 90s or whatever playing Tony Hawk Pro Skater 1.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.660
And then we pick up Tony Hawk Pro Skater 2.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:06.580
It's like a Crash Bandicoot style 3D platformer on a skateboard instead of like, yes, do 30 second sessions or 60 second sessions and do tricks.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:13.540
Yeah. The the I can totally understand like making it more of a story mode.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.360
But you have to keep something.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:22.740
And they even changed like just the basic like they changed the basic mechanics of the game.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:23.560
Yeah.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:28.080
And the like it used to be kind of overhead and had this faux 3D.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:33.760
And now it's more of a side scroller where you can kind of move on the Z axis.

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:36.020
But yeah, it's a weird thing.

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:39.640
Talk about that. Because they did the way you control the skateboard.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.140
It just takes some getting used to.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:52.180
I'm not saying it's wrong, but it's not necessarily the way like when I first picked up the game, I would have just assumed that I can just use the up, down, left, right buttons on the D pad.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:54.140
No, yeah. To move in those directions.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:55.320
But that's not how it works.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:18:00.960
No, it's kind of like it's a simulation of being bad at skateboarding.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:06.660
You know, you have to use the directional buttons left or right.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.600
You can't start up or down.

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:09.640
That's against the rules.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:11.540
You have to go left or right.

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:14.560
And you have to kick off several times to get some speed.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:19.040
Then I guess the motor kicks in and you don't have to kick off anymore.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:26.480
But and then you can either shoot your paintball gun, which isn't explained that you have.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.160
And that or you can jump.

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:34.520
And it's it's doesn't it.

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:41.320
Whatever that like 3D feeling or that omnidirectional feeling from the original game, it's just not there anymore.

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:54.400
Yeah, it's like on one on some level, if you don't think about it hard enough, it makes a little bit of sense that you can't go up or down without going forward without having that momentum.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:59.040
And I know on a real skateboard, you could probably like, you know, do that thing where you tilt it back and turn.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:01.020
But, you know, they're not going to program in there.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.980
It makes it makes some sense.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:09.840
But I think that I think that what's missing here is that like balance between realism and fun.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:13.420
As far as the movement goes, like, yeah, maybe that's more realistic.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.860
But like, is it actually fun to do that in a video game to do it that way?

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:18.220
And that's what's frustrating me.

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:21.900
Like, I just want to go into this, go into this bookstore or whatever.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:25.300
You have to like do a K turn to even get up.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:29.700
Yeah. Or like I stopped because I almost passed it and this is my destination.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:34.460
And now that I stopped, yeah, I've got to like loop back around so I'm moving so I can go up.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.720
I can't just get us press up and go through the door.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:20:05.360
I can't just go through the door.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:11.900
And, you know, maybe I just wanted to maybe I just wanted this to be more of a sports game and less of an adventure game.

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:21.560
But like there isn't much about like skateboarding, like the skateboarding is just your method of movement in the world.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:30.880
There's not like a lot of like, you know, oh, and then grind on this rail to get to this area or launch up this half pipe to reach the next stage.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:36.000
You know, it's like it is just very much a use your paint.

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:37.380
It's a paintball gun, right?

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:49.620
Use your paintball gun to like, you know, fight back against enemies and and, you know, find out where you need to ultimately go to fight the quote unquote boss of the level.

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:56.480
That just makes it feel like another one of these action games, not necessarily like a skateboarding game.

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:57.820
Make sense? Yeah.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:07.680
Yeah, I think that our idea of what a skateboarding game is, is just so colored by Tony Hawk that like we can't even think outside the bounds of it.

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:13.580
Like just like your example of, oh, grind up this rail to go to this area.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:28.640
Like, I don't think that I've ever seen a real grind like in in a real like a real skateboarder performing a grind go more than like 20 feet off of like a, you know, like a.

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:36.760
It just like our idea of what a grind is, is this cartoon Tony Hawk version that never existed.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:40.240
Yeah. I mean, I see that for sure.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:43.540
Like, yeah, you don't you don't just stick to the rail and grind for 20 minutes.

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:55.280
But but the what it is for me, what like where I agree with what you're saying, Mike, is that it's the physics where it's like I want to feel like I'm moving on a skateboard, whether or not I'm doing tricks or whatever.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:56.740
Like it just doesn't feel like that.

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:58.180
This feels like you're trudging along.

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:01.960
Like I want to I don't know, I want to feel like I'm skating and dodging things.

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:03.520
And like, yes, you are dodging things here.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:04.620
But like you might as well.

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:08.040
I don't know. I shouldn't say you might as well be walking because there is that momentum.

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:19.540
But it's such a trudge that it doesn't feel like when you think about skateboarding, even when you're not thinking about like skateboarding in a video game, you think about skateboarding, you think about like moving fast and this fluid, smooth movement, maybe doing some tricks.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.520
And I know there's like technically tricks in this game.

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:26.940
But like, I don't know, does it ever feel like you're getting that adrenaline of skateboarding?

00:22:26.940 --> 00:22:29.260
But it's also not necessary to do those tricks.

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:36.980
Like you think about in the next stage after you kill or dispose of a man's wife.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:38.100
Let's just go with kill. Yeah.

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:42.960
Then you're in the mall and, you know, it changes the game a little bit.

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:49.160
Right now you're like, you know, I don't want to say I'd be generous if I call it like crazy taxi like.

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:55.440
But, you know, you're a delivery guy and you got to like go from one area, one shop to the next, like delivering the things in time.

00:22:56.780 --> 00:23:00.220
But there's no like you're just moving left to right.

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:03.860
Like I suppose like you have to avoid those shoppers.

00:23:04.140 --> 00:23:06.500
But it's not like I don't know.

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:15.500
It's not it almost loses the action part of the game, too, and just becomes more of this like, OK, go here, then go here, then go back here, then go back to this place, then go to this new place.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.440
Like just you just you're just kind of to your point.

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:24.100
You're not doing anything with the skateboard other than using it to kind of like glide across them all.

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:35.020
Yeah. I'd say like maybe Skate or Die 2 is to skateboarding as Paperboy is to BMX.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:38.480
It just seems to be a means to an end.

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:41.760
Paperboy has a great BMX section at the end, though.

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:45.020
Remember at the end of the stage, you have to go to the obstacle course.

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:52.280
But yeah, and that's like but that's true, though, because like Paperboy, you could almost have the same complaint.

00:23:52.420 --> 00:23:54.480
It doesn't really like feel like you're on this bike.

00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:56.380
But yeah, like that's not the point.

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.180
This is called Skate or Die.

00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:00.300
So like I want to feel like I'm on a skateboard.

00:24:00.300 --> 00:24:04.360
Well, I also want to feel like I'm being like like a rebel.

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:10.440
I mean, skateboarding was just banned and I don't have like a wanted meter as I'm skating through the town.

00:24:10.460 --> 00:24:11.740
You know, like where are the cops?

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:15.720
Like, yeah, it doesn't seem like you get a job.

00:24:16.080 --> 00:24:19.520
Right. It doesn't seem like I'm doing the or die part, you know?

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:27.100
Yeah. And then, yeah, level two, the guy is like, well, you're going to have to get a job.

00:24:27.280 --> 00:24:28.460
And he's like, this is war.

00:24:28.660 --> 00:24:29.800
And then you go get a job.

00:24:30.460 --> 00:24:35.140
I think it's more again, this is more about skateboarding culture than it is about skateboarding.

00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:44.720
So like you were just working at Zoomies like like any other mid aughts skateboard kid would do.

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:52.700
Yeah. But, you know, speaking of the job that you have now, you're delivering stuff within the mall.

00:24:53.140 --> 00:24:55.540
But like you're delivering from like one mall store to another.

00:24:55.540 --> 00:25:02.280
So like the record store has to deliver something to the healthy food store, which then is like, great, deliver this to the shoeshine place.

00:25:02.440 --> 00:25:04.500
And what products are they are changing?

00:25:04.680 --> 00:25:06.060
What is this economy in this mall?

00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:09.720
Maybe all their stuff got mixed up and they're hoping that you can sort it all out.

00:25:09.760 --> 00:25:15.700
Yeah, maybe. I think it's just more CDs, mixtapes, pizza and tacos.

00:25:17.440 --> 00:25:20.280
Balancing the stockpiles.

00:25:20.980 --> 00:25:40.820
Right. Well, since we're hungry for the skateboarding aspect of the game, it is worth noting that after you complete the game or whatever, what you're building towards essentially is getting the blueprints and then the building, the construction of this half pipe.

00:25:41.660 --> 00:25:45.280
Which is called Double Trouble, which is interesting.

00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:50.320
I would have thought Double Trouble, the search for Double Trouble, I wouldn't think would be the half pipe for some reason.

00:25:50.460 --> 00:25:52.760
I would have thought that was like, I don't know.

00:25:52.880 --> 00:25:54.640
I guess I didn't think about what that would be.

00:25:55.200 --> 00:25:58.940
Well, because it doesn't really come up in the story until like halfway through the game.

00:25:59.100 --> 00:26:00.460
Because at first it's like skateboarding is banned.

00:26:00.580 --> 00:26:02.300
Which is fine. And then it's like the half pipe is destroyed.

