00:26:37.360 --> 00:26:40.520
I think it's very much required.

00:26:40.520 --> 00:26:48.080
I understand what you're getting at where like, you know, that kind of undercuts any level of accomplishment that you might feel here.

00:26:48.080 --> 00:27:06.220
But I'd say that the half pipe is much more fun than the standard mode, even though it is a completely different play style and actually lends itself to those more like run based mini games.

00:27:06.220 --> 00:27:12.120
So I think they had to just to just to have anybody want to pick up the game a second time.

00:27:13.120 --> 00:27:16.620
Yeah, because here you can actually, you know, I mean, it's a big half pipe.

00:27:17.500 --> 00:27:18.920
I thought it was pretty impressive.

00:27:19.620 --> 00:27:22.680
Not in the sense of like, wow, I'd like to see that thing in real life.

00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:36.120
But like for a video game, like, you know, like I think like it actually did get the skateboarding job done here and make you like feel the momentum of going up this half pipe and then skating all the way over to the other side and kind of building this momentum.

00:27:36.120 --> 00:27:42.560
And then like you can do cool tricks here that I would have liked to have had like some kind of use in the game for.

00:27:42.700 --> 00:27:48.280
Right. Like it's kind of weird that you don't attack enemies with a kickflip and instead you use a paintball gun.

00:27:48.960 --> 00:27:51.260
Yeah. Attack with a kickflip.

00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:54.720
But the I felt the same way at first.

00:27:54.840 --> 00:28:03.020
Like, OK, this feels like a really good like the physics of this feel good compared to like I can't really remember exactly what it was like to play Skate or Die 1.

00:28:03.200 --> 00:28:05.460
But I feel like I didn't remember thinking the physics were as good.

00:28:06.120 --> 00:28:10.080
But then I think then this is not a knock against Skate or Die 2.

00:28:10.300 --> 00:28:25.700
I think I am just poorly like my expectations are colored by 3D world skateboarding games, you know, by Tony Hawk or even just other games of like three dimensional physics.

00:28:26.440 --> 00:28:32.060
Where I as much as like this is great for its time, it's just that it's great for its time.

00:28:32.300 --> 00:28:35.760
It doesn't. And, you know, maybe it's just me because it's what I grew up with.

00:28:35.760 --> 00:28:43.420
And like maybe if you're if you're more if you grew up with NES games and you're more used to that, like, are you you know, you were you remember these?

00:28:43.560 --> 00:28:45.800
